{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["iOS","iPadOS","Mac Catalyst"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"@interface"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNPolygon"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"c:objc(cs)MLNMultiPoint","text":"MLNMultiPoint","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPoint"}],"languages":["occ"]}]},{"mentions":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/GeoJSON","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre-Native-for-iOS\/Predicates_and_Expressions"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can add polygon shapes to the map by adding them to an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"object. Configure the appearance of an "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNShapeSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s polygons collectively using an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNVectorTileSource"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNSymbolStyleLayer"},{"type":"text","text":" object. To access a polygon’s attributes, use an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygonFeature"},{"type":"text","text":" object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Alternatively, you can add a polygon overlay directly to a map view using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/addAnnotation:","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapView\/addOverlay:","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method. Configure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a polygon overlay’s appearance using"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapViewDelegate\/mapView:strokeColorForShapeAnnotation:"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMapViewDelegate\/mapView:fillColorForPolygonAnnotation:"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The vertices are automatically connected in the order in which you provide"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them. You should close the polygon by specifying the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" as the first and last vertices; otherwise, the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"polygon’s fill may not cover the area you expect it to. To avoid filling the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"space within the shape, give the polygon a transparent fill or use an"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolyline"},{"type":"text","text":" object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A polygon may have one or more interior polygons, or holes, that you specify as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"text":" objects with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+polygonWithCoordinates:count:interiorPolygons:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method. For example, if a polygon represents a lake, it could exclude an island"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within the lake using an interior polygon. Interior polygons may not themselves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"have interior polygons. To represent a shape that includes a polygon within a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hole or, more generally, to group multiple polygons together in one shape, use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon"},{"type":"text","text":" object."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To make the polygon straddle the antimeridian, specify some longitudes less","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"than −180 degrees or greater than 180 degrees.","type":"text"}]},{"level":4,"text":"Related examples","type":"heading","anchor":"Related-examples"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"TODO: Add a polygon annotation, learn how to initialize an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},{"text":" object from an array of coordinates.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" object represents a closed shape consisting of four or more","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices, specified as ","type":"text"},{"code":"CLLocationCoordinate2D","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" instances, and the edges that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connect them. For example, you could use a polygon shape to represent a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"building, a lake, or an area you want to highlight.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"occ"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/maplibre\/mlnpolygon"]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"occ","url":"doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon"},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Class","externalID":"c:objc(cs)MLNPolygon","role":"symbol","title":"MLNPolygon","modules":[{"name":"MapLibre"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNPolygon"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MLNPolygon"}],"symbolKind":"class"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre"]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Instance-Properties","title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/interiorPolygons"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Type-Methods","title":"Type Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/polygonWithCoordinates:count:","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNPolygon\/polygonWithCoordinates:count:interiorPolygons:"],"generated":true}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Shapes","title":"Shapes","identifiers":["doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNEmptyFeature","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPoint","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygon","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/documentation\/MapLibre\/MLNMultiPolygonFeature","doc:\/\/org.swift.MyProject\/docu